Thus plan steps:

1. Detach task profile from destination_availability_alpha (detach_task_profile) to make route_task_profile_available.
2. Attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha (attach_task_profile).
3. Confirm candidate preparedness for origin_availability_alpha (confirm_candidate_preparedness).
4. Optionally detach task profile from origin_availability_alpha (detach_task_profile) to free profile for shift_candidate_beta.
5. Attach task profile to shift_candidate_beta (attach_task_profile).
6. Confirm candidate preparedness for shift_candidate_beta.
7. Assign operator resource to origin_availability_alpha (assign_operator_resource) for lock.
8. Activate origin node (activate_origin_node) using origin_availability_alpha and route_task_profile_alpha? Wait activate_origin_node requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile. So we need origin_availability_alpha to have task profile linked at time of activation. So we cannot detach before activation. Actually activate_origin_node requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile. So we need origin_availability_alpha linked to a task profile when we activate. So we need to keep link during activation. After activation, we can detach if needed.

